Wire the Nax agent + sidecar into the AdaptixServer workspace (go.work).

The Nax server plugin (NaX/src_server/agent_nonameax) resolves the sidecar
builder through a local replace in its go.mod: the module path
sidecar/nax-builder is pinned to ../../../sidecar/nax-builder. Listing both
the Nax agent and the sidecar in go.work's use list makes the Go toolchain
(and `go work sync`) resolve that replacement.

go.work is not tracked in the AdaptixC2 submodule commit, so it is generated
in the Docker build stage by `go work use ... && go work sync` (see the
build-server stage). This patch therefore targets an EXISTING go.work
(e.g. after `go work init` or a prior build) — the local-build / manual-checkout
path. It reproduces, verbatim, the entries that stage adds inline, so the two
stay in sync.

diff --git a/AdaptixServer/go.work b/AdaptixServer/go.work
index 0000000..0000000
--- a/AdaptixServer/go.work
+++ b/AdaptixServer/go.work
@@ -9,4 +9,9 @@
 	./extenders/beacon_listener_tcp
 	./extenders/gopher_agent
 	./extenders/gopher_listener_tcp
+	// Nax agent module (submodule) — payload generation now talks to the
+	// sidecar builder over a unix socket. Its go.mod pins the sidecar via a
+	// local replace, so both this module and the sidecar are listed here.
+	../../NaX/src_server/agent_nonameax
+	../../sidecar/nax-builder
 )
